From b8ecedac80d2f732ae7d1ff611c9ee1e4ac38cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ys-ll <114486081+ys-ll@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:45:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rdp: implement standard RDP security (RC4) client support

Implement the legacy pre-TLS RC4 encryption layer (PROTOCOL_RDP) so the
client can connect to servers that only offer standard RDP security,
such as xrdp configured with security_layer=rdp or servers with a
broken TLS setup.

- pdu: add the standard RDP security crypto module (session key
  derivation, MAC, RC4 streams with 4096-packet key rollover, 40/56/128
  bit keys; FIPS rejected), the Security Exchange PDU, and secured
  share-data encoders
- connector: accept a PROTOCOL_RDP selection, advertise RC4 encryption
  methods in GCC, add the Security Exchange phase, seal the Client Info
  PDU, decrypt inbound envelopes, and thread the security context
  through activation/finalization and the connection result
- session: decrypt slow-path and fast-path inbound payloads, seal
  outbound share data, static channel chunks and fast-path input
- web: accept standard RDP security as an additional fallback while
  still advertising SSL/HYBRID
